# Baseline for subject-annotation mismatches in internal hash citations.
# The gate reports ADVISORY for entries listed here; any new subject mismatch
# not present in this file is a FAIL.  This is a descend-only ratchet:
# removing a mismatch (by correcting the annotation) removes its entry;
# adding a new wrong annotation fails immediately.
#
# Format: file:hashtoken
#
# The annotated subject must match `git log -1 --pretty=%s <hash>` exactly.
# To clear an entry: correct the ("annotation") in the cited line to the
# real commit subject and remove the corresponding line from this file in
# the same commit.
#
# --- current known mismatches ---
#
# include/cmp_hints/redqueen.h:90
#   annotated: "drain all staged reexec_pending entries per dispatch"
#   real:      "random-syscall: drain all staged reexec_pending entries per dispatch"
#   (annotation is missing the "random-syscall:" subsystem prefix)
include/cmp_hints/redqueen.h:b86f2e77a846
